      "slug": "journey-with-spring-boot",
      "title": "Diving into Spring Boot: Why Java for Enterprise Backends",
      "date": "2026-10-18",
      "tags": [
        "spring-boot",
        "java",
        "backend"
      ],
      "summary": "Exploring dependency injection, JPA/Hibernate, and building robust REST services.",
      "minutes": 2,
      "content": "### Why Spring Boot?\n\nAs someone passionate about building scalable backends, moving from Node.js and Express to **Spring Boot** opened up an entire world of enterprise software patterns.\n\n#### Key Learnings So Far:\n- **Dependency Injection & Inversion of Control**: How Spring manages bean lifecycle cleanly.\n- **Spring Data JPA**: Simplifying data access with repositories without boilerplate JDBC code.\n- **REST Architecture**: Clean separation between Controllers, Services, and Repositories.\n\nSpring Boot provides the rock-solid structure and type safety that large distributed systems require."
    },
    {
      "slug": "leetcode-350-insights",
      "title": "What Solving 350+ LeetCode Questions Taught Me",
      "date": "2026-09-25",
      "tags": [
        "dsa",
        "leetcode",
        "algorithms"
      ],
      "summary": "Key takeaways on problem breakdown, pattern recognition, and consistency.",
      "minutes": 2,
      "content": "### Consistency Over Intensity\n\nCrossing the 350+ problems mark on LeetCode taught me that problem solving isn't about memorizing solutions—it's about **pattern recognition**.\n\n#### The Big Patterns:\n- **Two Pointers & Sliding Window** for substring and array subarray problems.\n- **BFS vs DFS**: When to traverse level-by-level vs deep path exploration.\n- **Dynamic Programming**: Breaking down subproblems and defining transition states.\n\nDaily consistency beats weekend cramming every single time."
    },
    {
      "slug": "first-open-source-pr",
      "title": "Getting My First Open Source PRs Merged",
      "date": "2026-10-17",
      "tags": [
        "open-source",
